  "simplified": [
    "Main cables use a smoothed six-sided section, enlarged to 1.64 m across. Suspenders use a square 1.10 m display section at 15.24 m intervals.",
    "A 7.62 m deep stiffening web uses 15.24 m panels and alternating 45° diagonals. The profile uses a simplified 1.5 m crown-to-upper-chord allowance.",
    "Legs step back on their outer faces with vertical inner jambs. Recessed channels replace finer fluting on the legs and cross struts. Each cable seats between a pair of saddle cheeks.",
    "Vertical plinths run under the land anchorages to mean sea level. Each approach terminates on an open, grounded two-leg bent with a cap and diagonal. Four Fort Point ribs retain their separate springings.",
    "Lights, guardrail pickets, safety netting, road markings, terrain and water are omitted.",
    "A raised fender rim, grouped arch posts and a cap course on the southern housing distinguish the shore supports at map scale.",
    "One movable maintenance traveler is shown at midspan for the clearance comparison. Its location varies in service."
  ],
